cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Frankl's union-closed sets conjecture under cyclic symmetry: SAT-certified results for Z13 and Z14"
authors:
  - family-names: Albanese
    given-names: Simone
type: software
date-released: 2026-08-12
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Computer-assisted decision of the rotation-invariant case of Frankl's
  union-closed sets conjecture. No rotation-invariant counterexample exists on
  13 or 14 points: both cases are decided by two independent exact methods and
  carry DRAT certificates verified with drat-trim. The 15-point case is decided
  by one exact method (CP-SAT, infeasible) and left honestly unconfirmed, with
  a reproducible pipeline, measured resource costs, and a concrete plan for
  completing it. The search itself was executed autonomously by an AI agent
  loop built on Anthropic's Claude Code (model Claude Fable 5) under human
  supervision.
